===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[subsidiary]] [[entrance]] to a [[building]] or [[house]] at its rear, normally away from the [[street]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2023 January 11|author=Stephen Roberts|title=Bradshaw's Britain: castles and cathedrals|journal=RAIL|issue=974|page=57|text="Charles II, who was crowned here a little while before, occupied an old house (which is still standing) in New Street [Worcester], from which he escaped by the '''back door''', as the enemy rushed in at the front."}}
# A means of [[access]], often secret and unprotected, to something.
#* {{quote-web|en|date=29 November 2021|author=w:Alan Shearer|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/59448217|work=BBC Sport|title=Why Newcastle have to win their next two games to give them hope of staying in the Premier League - Alan Shearer analysis|passage=Scoring three goals at home should guarantee you three points, but when you go on the attack a little bit more, you leave the '''back door''' open. That's not always a good idea with this team.}}
# {{lb|en|computer security}} A secret means of access to a [[program]] or [[system]].
# {{lb|en|automotive}} A rear side door of a car, or at the back of a [[van]].
# {{lb|en|slang}} The [[anus]]; {{lb|en|by extension}} [[anal sex]].
#: {{syn|en|backgate}}
#: {{coi|en|'''backdoor''' action}}
#: {{coi|en|go up the '''back door'''}}
#* {{quote-av|en|writer=Michael Patrick King|title=w:Sex and the City|episode=Valley of the Twenty-Something Guys|date=June 28, 1998|season=1|number=4|role=Samantha|passage= Oh, don't be so judgmental. You could use a little '''back door'''.}}
# {{lb|en|golf|informal}} The rear side of the hole, furthest from the golfer.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2010|author=Bob Glanville|title=Golf: The Game of Lessening Failures|page=14
|passage=Sometimes the ball will curve around and enter from the '''back-door'''.}}

